// Patching (docs/patching.md): assemble a line at an address, patch
// instructions and bytes, list and revert patches, and export the patched
// file with checksum fixups. Added in api_minor 27 (feature "patch").
//
// A patch is an assertion (FACT_KIND_PATCH at its first byte, the new bytes
// as its value, at most 256 bytes; longer edits are several), so it has
// provenance, blame, history, undo (RetractAssertions), bulk revert
// (RevertByProvenance) and replication like every other edit. Every view
// that decodes the program's bytes (discovery, the listing, instructions,
// graphs, xrefs, decompilation, the emulator, analyzer plugins) reads them
// as patched; the file's own bytes never change.

